// eu-sovereign — EU data beyond the reach of non-EU surveillance law
//
// The law: after Schrems II (CJEU C-311/18), a transfer is lawful only if
// the data is protected from foreign access in practice, not just on paper.
// Laws such as US FISA §702 and the CLOUD Act let authorities compel a
// provider headquartered there, wherever its servers are.
//
// This pack: everything stays in the EU, and no offer within reach of US,
// Chinese or Russian law is allowed unless you hold the encryption keys,
// so that compelled access yields only ciphertext.
//
// Use `import "eu-sovereign"`, alone or with "gdpr". Not legal advice.

policy eu-sovereign {
  residency          = eu
  min_trust          = T2
  deny jurisdictions = [ us, cn, ru ]
}
